<title>UK: AMP denies Virgin/Bank of Scotland talks.</title>
<headline>AMP denies Virgin/Bank of Scotland talks.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Mutual Provident Society (AMP) on Tuesday denied reports that AMP and Virgin Direct were about to enter a joint venture with Bank of Scotland to launch a direct banking operation in the UK.</p>
<p>James Willoughby, chief manager corporate affairs, said that remarks attributed to AMP were incorrect.</p>
<p>&quot;AMP is in talks with Virgin to inject a further 290 million pounds to enable Virgin Direct to build on its success to date of attracting one billion pounds from 200,000 customers in nearly 2-1/2 years,&quot; said Willoughby.</p>
<p>&quot;However, neither AMP or Virgin are in negotiations with Bank of Scotland.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
